{
  "format": 1,
  "doc": "tutorials/multi_contrast",
  "id": "multi-contrast",
  "title": "Fitting several contrasts",
  "example": "",
  "data": [
    "film_contrasts.ort"
  ],
  "minutes": 15,
  "summary": "Build a film model from a data file, make two more water contrasts and fit all three together.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "title": "Three waters, one film",
      "body": "This tutorial starts from an empty project. You will build the model of a film on silicon in\nD₂O from a data file, make two more contrasts of it in H₂O and in silicon-matched water\n(CMSi), load the three measurements and fit them together with one structure.",
      "page": "project",
      "sidebarTab": "",
      "target": "",
      "done": "",
      "actions": [],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#the-film-in-three-waters"
    },
    {
      "id": "open-sample",
      "title": "Open the Sample page",
      "body": "Open the **Sample** page with its tab in the application bar.",
      "page": "",
      "sidebarTab": "",
      "target": "appbar.sampleTab",
      "done": "ui.page == 'sample'",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "goto",
          "args": [
            "sample"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": true,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#build-one-model"
    },
    {
      "id": "load-sample",
      "title": "Load the model from the data file",
      "body": "In **Load a sample**, untick **Append to existing models**, press **Load sample from file**\nand pick `film_contrasts.ort`; the file dialog opens in the folder of the tutorial's data.\nThe model is Si | SiO2 | Film | D2O, built from the file header. With **Append** left\nticked, the empty project's model stays next to it: restart the tutorial then.",
      "page": "sample",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "sample.loadSample",
      "done": "models.count == 1 and sample.material_slds.get('SiO2', 0) > 3",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "project.sampleLoad",
            "{data}/film_contrasts.ort",
            false
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#build-one-model"
    },
    {
      "id": "rename-model",
      "title": "Name the model",
      "body": "In the **Models selector**, rename the model to `Film in D2O`. It will be the reference\nfor the other contrasts.",
      "page": "sample",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "sample.models",
      "done": "models.names.count('Film in D2O') == 1",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "sample.setModelNameAtIndex",
            0,
            "Film in D2O"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#build-one-model"
    },
    {
      "id": "rename-assembly",
      "title": "Name the assembly",
      "body": "In the **Model editor**, rename the assembly `Loaded layer`, which holds the oxide and the\nfilm, to `Oxide and film`.",
      "page": "sample",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "sample.assemblies",
      "done": "sample.assemblies.count('Oxide and film') == 1",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "sample.setAssemblyNameAtIndex",
            1,
            "Oxide and film"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#build-one-model"
    },
    {
      "id": "waters",
      "title": "Make the other two waters",
      "body": "In the **Material editor**, press **Add material** twice. Name the new rows `H2O` with SLD\n`-0.56` and `CMSi` with SLD `2.07`.",
      "page": "sample",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "sample.addMaterial",
      "done": "abs(sample.material_slds.get('H2O', 9) + 0.56) < 0.001 and abs(sample.material_slds.get('CMSi', 0) - 2.07) < 0.001",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "click",
          "args": [
            "sample.addMaterial"
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "click",
          "args": [
            "sample.addMaterial"
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "sample.setMaterialNameAtIndex",
            4,
            "H2O"
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "sample.setMaterialSldAtIndex",
            4,
            -0.56
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "sample.setMaterialNameAtIndex",
            5,
            "CMSi"
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "sample.setMaterialSldAtIndex",
            5,
            2.07
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#build-one-model"
    },
    {
      "id": "contrast-h2o",
      "title": "Add the H2O contrast",
      "body": "With `Film in D2O` selected in the **Models selector**, press\n**Add contrast of the selected model…**. Name the new model `Film in H2O`, replace `D2O`\nwith `H2O`, leave the other materials at `keep`, and press **OK**.",
      "page": "sample",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "sample.addContrast",
      "done": "models.names.count('Film in H2O') == 1",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "sample.contrastCandidates",
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "sample.addContrast",
            0,
            "Film in H2O",
            [
              {
                "candidate": 3,
                "material": 4
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#make-the-other-contrasts-with-add-contrast"
    },
    {
      "id": "contrast-cmsi",
      "title": "Add the CMSi contrast",
      "body": "The new model is now the selected one, so select `Film in D2O` again first. Then add a\ncontrast named `Film in CMSi` that replaces `D2O` with `CMSi`.",
      "page": "sample",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "sample.addContrast",
      "done": "models.names.count('Film in CMSi') == 1",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "sample.contrastCandidates",
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "sample.addContrast",
            0,
            "Film in CMSi",
            [
              {
                "candidate": 3,
                "material": 5
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#make-the-other-contrasts-with-add-contrast"
    },
    {
      "id": "shared",
      "title": "What the contrasts share",
      "body": "In the **Model editor**, the superphase and `Oxide and film` are marked **⇄**: the three\nmodels share them, so they have one film thickness between them. Each model has its own\nsubphase, with its own water, and its own scale and background.",
      "page": "sample",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "sample.assemblies",
      "done": "",
      "actions": [],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#make-the-other-contrasts-with-add-contrast"
    },
    {
      "id": "load-data",
      "title": "Load the three measurements",
      "body": "On the **Experiment** page, press **Load experiment(s) from file(s)** and pick\n`film_contrasts.ort` again. The file holds three datasets, so you get three experiments.",
      "page": "experiment",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "experiment.loadData",
      "done": "experiments.count >= 3",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "experiment.load",
            "{data}/film_contrasts.ort"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#load-the-data-and-pair-it-with-the-models"
    },
    {
      "id": "pair",
      "title": "Pair each measurement with its contrast",
      "body": "All three experiments start with the same model. In the **Model** column of the\n**Data Explorer**, give the D2O data `Film in D2O`, the H2O data `Film in H2O` and the CMSi\ndata `Film in CMSi`. A wrong pairing gives a bad fit without an error message.",
      "page": "experiment",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "experiment.dataExplorer",
      "done": "experiments.models == ['Film in D2O', 'Film in H2O', 'Film in CMSi']",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setModelOnExperiment",
            0,
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setModelOnExperiment",
            1,
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setModelOnExperiment",
            2,
            2
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#load-the-data-and-pair-it-with-the-models"
    },
    {
      "id": "fit-flags",
      "title": "Choose the parameters to fit",
      "body": "On the **Analysis** page, tick **Fit** for exactly these: `SiO2 thickness`,\n`Film thickness`, `Film sld`, `Film roughness` and the three scales, and untick the rest.\nThe shared parameters are one row each, marked **⇄**. The new waters arrive with their\n`sld` and `isld` ticked: untick them, as the water SLDs are known.",
      "page": "analysis",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "analysis.parameterTable",
      "done": "params.free == 7 and params.is_free('sio2_thickness') and params.is_free('film_thickness') and params.is_free('film_sld') and params.is_free('film_roughness') and params.is_free('film_in_d2o_scale') and params.is_free('film_in_h2o_scale') and params.is_free('film_in_cmsi_scale')",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "sio2_thickness",
            true
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "film_thickness",
            true
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "film_sld",
            true
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "film_roughness",
            true
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "film_in_d2o_scale",
            true
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "film_in_h2o_scale",
            true
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "film_in_cmsi_scale",
            true
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "h2o_sld",
            false
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "h2o_isld",
            false
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "cmsi_sld",
            false
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "cmsi_isld",
            false
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterFit",
            "film_in_d2o_subphase_roughness",
            false
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#fit-the-three-contrasts-together"
    },
    {
      "id": "backgrounds",
      "title": "Set the backgrounds",
      "body": "Set the backgrounds to `2e-7` (`Film in D2O`), `5e-6` (`Film in H2O`) and `1e-6`\n(`Film in CMSi`), and keep them fixed. The data are simulated, so these are known.",
      "page": "analysis",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "analysis.parameterTable",
      "done": "abs(params.value('film_in_d2o_background') - 2e-7) < 1e-9 and abs(params.value('film_in_h2o_background') - 5e-6) < 1e-8 and abs(params.value('film_in_cmsi_background') - 1e-6) < 1e-8",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterValue",
            "film_in_d2o_background",
            2e-07
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterValue",
            "film_in_h2o_background",
            5e-06
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterValue",
            "film_in_cmsi_background",
            1e-06
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#fit-the-three-contrasts-together"
    },
    {
      "id": "start-values",
      "title": "Start from the wrong structure",
      "body": "The model still has the values the file was simulated with. Move them away, so the fit has\nsomething to find: oxide thickness `25`, film thickness `70`, film SLD `1` and film\nroughness `3`.",
      "page": "analysis",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "analysis.parameterTable",
      "done": "abs(params.value('sio2_thickness') - 25) < 0.5 and abs(params.value('film_thickness') - 70) < 0.5 and abs(params.value('film_sld') - 1) < 0.01 and abs(params.value('film_roughness') - 3) < 0.1",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterValue",
            "sio2_thickness",
            25
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterValue",
            "film_thickness",
            70
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterValue",
            "film_sld",
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setParameterValue",
            "film_roughness",
            3
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#fit-the-three-contrasts-together"
    },
    {
      "id": "fit",
      "title": "Fit the three contrasts together",
      "body": "Leave **Fit** ticked for all three experiments in the **Data Explorer** and press\n**Start fitting**. The joint fit finds the oxide at about 15.2 Å and the film at 80.0 Å,\nwith SLD 2.00 and roughness 5.0 Å, at a reduced χ² of about 0.89.",
      "page": "analysis",
      "sidebarTab": "",
      "target": "analysis.startFitting",
      "done": "step.fits_finished >= 1 and fit.reduced_chi2 < 1.5",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "click",
          "args": [
            "analysis.startFitting"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "The fit did not find the structure. Check the pairing in the Data Explorer and the parameters ticked for fitting.",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#fit-the-three-contrasts-together"
    },
    {
      "id": "results",
      "title": "Read the results",
      "body": "The **Refinement Results** dialog lists each dataset with its χ² per point and its share\nof the total, all three close to 1. Press **OK**.",
      "page": "analysis",
      "sidebarTab": "",
      "target": "",
      "done": "not fit.results_dialog_open",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "analysis.setShowFitResultsDialog",
            false
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#fit-the-three-contrasts-together"
    },
    {
      "id": "detach",
      "title": "Let one parameter differ in one contrast",
      "body": "Select the `Film roughness` row. Below the table, pick `Film in CMSi` after\n**Detach in** and press **Detach**. `Film in CMSi` now has its own copy of\n`Oxide and film`, and its film roughness is a row of its own, `Film in CMSi Film roughness`.\nEvery other parameter of the copy still follows the shared one.",
      "page": "analysis",
      "sidebarTab": "basic",
      "target": "analysis.parameterTable",
      "done": "params.has('film_in_cmsi_film_roughness')",
      "actions": [
        {
          "verb": "call",
          "args": [
            "sample.detachParameterByAlias",
            "film_roughness",
            2
          ]
        }
      ],
      "advance": false,
      "requires": "",
      "hint": "",
      "more": "tutorials/multi_contrast.html#let-one-parameter-differ-in-one-contrast"
    }
  ]
}
